 "summary_en": "HUS says it does its lung surgery at Meilahti Tower Hospital and that its multidisciplinary lung cancer team gives recommendations \"when needed\". No HUS or Päijät-Häme page we read says that a thoracic surgeon reviews Päijät-Häme's decisions not to operate. A study of England's national lung cancer audit (Lau et al., 2013) found that 20.0% of patients were operated on in hospitals with resident thoracic surgeons, against 11.6% in other hospitals; the study is observational.",
 "unanswered_en": "We found no public page describing Päijät-Häme's lung cancer meeting or a surgeon's part in it.",
